  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome to guide the choice, preferring lotteries without such sure outcomes. However, in this case, neither lottery has a sure outcome, so the reason would not generate a preference. The individual, in contrast, does not mention anything about certainty or sure outcomes. Instead, the individual focuses on the similarity of winning probabilities and chooses based on the higher payoff. There is no indication that the individual considered whether an outcome was certain or not. The information used by the individual (probabilities and payoff sizes) and the justification (favoring higher payoff under similar probabilities) do not align with the decision reason’s focus on sure outcomes. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
